So if $u, v \in V_{even}$, then $d(v) \le d(u) + 1$. Since $d(v)$ is even, $d(v)$ must be $\le d(u)$. Similarly $d(u) \le d(v)$. Thus $d(u) = d(v)$.
This means if there is an edge between two vertices in $V_{even}$, they must have the same shortest distance from 1.
Similarly, if there is an edge between two vertices in $V_{odd}$, they must have the same shortest distance from 1.
